[38;5;231m⏺[39m This is a one-line value change, but session lifetime is a security-posture setting, so I want your explicit yes
  before editing rather than after.

  [38;5;153mconfig.js:3[39m is [38;5;153mSESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30[39m, consumed by [38;5;153mserver.js[39m as the session expiry. Going to 480 makes a stolen
  or unattended session valid for a full workday instead of half an hour — 16x the window in which a hijacked session
  cookie, a shared machine, or an unlocked laptop stays usable. Nothing else in the repo compensates for that (no idle
  timeout, no re-auth on sensitive actions).

